      "observed": "The MCU VDD pins are explicitly unconnected rather than tied to the 3.3 V rail; FCC1 VDDA and NAVC1 VSSA are also unconnected. NAVC1 VBAT is on +3V3, but its VDD pins are not.",
      "expected": "Both MCU VDD pins should be powered from the 3.3 V rail, with the analog supply and ground pins connected appropriately. The specification states that 3.3 V feeds both MCUs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"VDD\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"VDD\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3 V feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "As represented, neither MCU receives power on its VDD pins, so the flight computers cannot operate; the unconnected analog supply/ground pins add further functional problems.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["HSE1", "HSE2", "FCC1", "NAVC1", "R23", "R32"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.5", "FCC1.37", "FCC1.12", "FCC1.13", "NAVC1.5", "NAVC1.6"],
      "nets": ["HSE_IN_FCC", "HSE_OUT_FCC", "HSE_IN_NAVC", "HSE_OUT_NAVC", "Net-(FCC1-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH1)"],
      "observed": "The FCC crystal circuitry connects to FCC1 pins 5 and 37, identified in the netlist as PE6 and PE7, while the MCU's PH0/PH1 pins are on separate nets. The NAVC crystal nets do not connect to NAVC1 at all; NAVC1 pins 5 and 6 (PH0/PH1) instead connect to capacitors.",
      "expected": "Each 25 MHz HSE crystal circuit should connect to its MCU's HSE oscillator pins (PH0/PH1), not unrelated GPIOs or isolated nets. The specification identifies an HSE crystal for both MCUs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\")) (node (ref \"HSE1\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_OUT_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_OUT_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"R32\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The NAVC external clock is disconnected from its MCU, and the FCC crystal is connected to non-oscillator pins. The MCUs may fail to start or run without the intended external clock, and the oscillator circuitry will not function as designed.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["FCC1", "UART3_FCC1", "C13"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.48", "FCC1.73", "UART3_FCC1.3", "UART3_FCC1.4"],
      "nets": ["UART3_TX_FCC", "UART3_RX_FCC", "unconnected-(C13-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "Both FCC1 VCAP pins are connected directly to UART3 connector pins: pin 48 to UART3_TX_FCC and pin 73 to UART3_RX_FCC. C13, a 2.2 µF capacitor, has one pad unconnected rather than serving those VCAP pins.",
      "expected": "The MCU VCAP pins require their specified core-regulator bypass capacitors and should not be used as UART signals. UART3 signals should connect to functional UART pins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"UART3_TX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC1\") (pin \"3\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"UART3_RX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC1\") (pin \"4\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(C13-Pad1)\") ... (node (ref \"C13\") (pin \"1\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The UART3 connector is driven by MCU core-supply output pins rather than UART signals, and the required VCAP decoupling is absent, potentially preventing correct MCU operation and risking damage or malfunction.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows fundamental MCU power and clock connectivity faults, plus FCC VCAP pins misused as UART3 signals. These are direct connectivity deviations that would prevent the board from behaving as intended."
}

